# EAIA → CRM Integration Plan (Actionable)

This rule is a concise, step-by-step plan to implement EAIA capabilities inside the CRM. It maps EAIA modules to CRM APIs, data model changes, UI, security, and testing. Use it to guide implementation and reviews.

## Current Status
- Completed
  - Core CRM email APIs: get_inbox, thread_context, save_draft, send, link_provider_ids
  - Agent router commands: email.draft, email.send, email.link_provider_ids, email.draft_with_provider (NEW)
  - Human Inbox web page `/human_inbox` with filters and Send action
  - Email Account configured and tested; outbound email working
  - Convenience API: `crm.api.email.save_draft_with_provider` to create a draft and set `provider*` IDs in one call
- Pending/Backlog
  - Configure SPF/DKIM/DMARC (deliverability)
  - EAIA service setup (OAuth, ingest, deploy/cron) and E2E wiring

## Scope
- AI triage, drafting, rewrite, and meeting scheduling via EAIA
- Gmail ingest/send + provider ID mapping on `Communication`
- Human-in-the-loop review in two places: `/human_inbox` and embedded in `/crm` dashboard + Lead detail
- Secure EAIA→CRM communication (API key/secret, allowlist) and least-privilege roles
- 360 AI dashboard inside `/crm` with live counters, quick actions, and drilldowns
- E2E tests for inbound→triage→draft→approve→send→track and deliverability checks
- Observability: logs, metrics, error alerts, email queue monitoring
- Deliverability & reputation (SPF/DKIM/DMARC) and warm-up guidance
- Governance: audit log of AI actions, approvals, and sends

## Target Capabilities (End State)
- AI Inbox Orchestration
  - Auto-triage recent inbound threads and draft replies when appropriate
  - Find meeting times, suggest/send calendar invites when requested
  - Respect user preferences from `config.yaml` (tone, scheduling rules)
- Embedded Assistant
  - `/crm` dashboard widget: Needs Triage, AI Drafts, Sent Today, Errors; quick actions
  - Lead/Contact page actions: AI Triage Thread, AI Draft Reply, Send; modal preview
- EAIA Integration
  - EAIA runs as external worker (local or LangGraph) and writes drafts via `email.draft_with_provider`
  - Provider IDs stored on `Communication` for cross-system linking
- Review & Approvals
  - Human review queue; send with one click; audit trail of who approved/sent
- Observability & Ops
  - Error notifications (API, Email Queue), dashboard counters, runbooks
  - Rate limits and backoff to avoid API exhaustion

## Phase 0 – Prereqs
- Configure Email Account in CRM (Gmail/IMAP+SMTP or provider)
- Ensure custom fields exist on `Communication`:
  - `provider` (Data), `provider_message_id` (Small Text), `provider_thread_id` (Small Text)
- Create dedicated EAIA API user with minimal permissions (read/write `Communication`, related DocTypes)

## Phase 1 – CRM Surface (Minimal API + Data Contracts)
- Add/confirm email endpoints in CRM:
  - get_inbox, thread_context, save_draft, send, link_provider_ids
  - Agent router: `crm.api.agent.run` supports: `email.draft`, `email.send`, `email.link_provider_ids`
- Ensure docs exist and are current: [docs/API_INDEX.md](mdc:crm-deployment/docs/API_INDEX.md)
- Validate provider fields are visible in Customize Form for `Communication`.

## Phase 2 – EAIA Service Setup
- In `assistant/executive-ai-assistant-main`:
  - Configure OAuth: run `scripts/setup_gmail.py` and store secrets under `eaia/.secrets`
  - Fill `eaia/main/config.yaml` with user preferences and email
  - Local run: `pip install -e . && langgraph dev`
  - Ingest: `python scripts/run_ingest.py --minutes-since 120 --rerun 1 --early 0`
- Optional: Deploy to LangGraph Platform; set `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and use `scripts/setup_cron.py` for scheduled ingest.

Acceptance criteria
- EAIA can authenticate to Gmail and fetch recent emails
- EAIA can run locally and in LangGraph Platform (optional)
- Secrets stored only in EAIA `.secrets` (not in CRM DB)

## Phase 3 – Wiring EAIA ↔ CRM
- Inbound (EAIA fetch → triage → draft):
  1) EAIA ingests Gmail, triages thread, drafts reply
  2) EAIA POSTs to CRM to create/update `Communication` using:
     - Preferred: `crm.api.agent.run` with `email.draft_with_provider` (one call) to create the draft and set `provider`, `provider_message_id`, `provider_thread_id`
     - Alternative (two calls): `email.draft` then `crm.api.email.link_provider_ids`
  3) CRM publishes realtime event to notify UI assignees (topic: `crm_email_draft_created`)
- Outbound (send):
  - Option A: CRM sends via `email.send` and optionally records provider IDs via a follow-up `email.link_provider_ids` if available
  - Option B: EAIA sends via Gmail API, then calls `email.link_provider_ids` to sync IDs in CRM

Acceptance criteria
- Drafts created by EAIA appear in `/human_inbox` and on the linked Lead/Contact
- Provider IDs visible on `Communication` and retrievable via API
- Sending works via CRM and/or EAIA with status reflected in CRM

## Phase 4 – Human Inbox UI (Review/Approve)
- Add web page under `crm/www/` to list:
  - Triaged items needing action
  - AI-generated drafts (status = Draft)
- Actions: view thread, edit draft, approve/send
- Subscribe to realtime `crm_email_draft_created` for auto-refresh

Embed in `/crm`
- Add AI Assistant widget with counters and links
- Add actions on Lead/Contact detail for AI triage/draft/send

Acceptance criteria
- `/human_inbox` shows items with filters and Send works
- `/crm` shows AI counters and links to filtered views
- Lead/Contact pages can create AI drafts and send from a modal

## Phase 5 – Notifications
- When a draft is created or triage requires attention, notify assignees via Desk notification and optional email
- Reuse existing `crm/api/notifications.py` where possible

Acceptance criteria
- Notifications created for targeted assignees when AI drafts/triage items arrive
- Users can click-through to the Communication or Lead

## Phase 6 – Security & Config
- Store EAIA→CRM credentials as API Key/Secret for EAIA user
- Optionally add IP allowlist (reverse proxy / WAF)
- Keep Gmail OAuth secrets in EAIA `.secrets` and never in CRM DB
- In CRM site config, store external LLM keys if used (e.g., `openai_api_key`)

Also
- Role for EAIA user limited to required DocTypes and endpoints
- Rate limits for inbound API; backoff on 429
- Audit log of AI actions (triage decisions, drafts, sends)

Acceptance criteria
- Security review passes (least privilege, secrets not leaked)
- API calls authenticated and rate-limited

## Phase 7 – E2E Tests & Ops
- Add test scripts in `crm-deployment/scripts/` to drive:
  - Draft creation → send → queue status verify
  - Thread context retrieval
  - Provider ID linking
- EAIA side: use `scripts/run_ingest.py` to simulate inbound; verify `Communication` creation
- Create a short-runbook in `docs/EAIA_E2E_TESTS.md` for operators

Acceptance criteria
- Green E2E run in staging
- Runbook covers restart, retries, and failure modes

## Phase 8 – Deliverability & Reputation (Backlog until ready)
- DNS: SPF, DKIM, DMARC for sending domain
- Warm-up schedule and content best practices
- Google Postmaster Tools and bounce/complaint monitoring

Acceptance criteria
- SPF/DKIM/DMARC = PASS on test headers
- Spam placement reduced on test accounts

## Phase 9 – Observability & Cost
- Logging: API errors, Email Queue failures
- Metrics: drafts/day, sends/day, triage outcomes, failure rates
- Cost controls: model selection, batching, rate caps

Acceptance criteria
- Dashboard or logs expose key KPIs
- Alerts on repeated failures or queue backlogs

## Data Contracts
- `Communication` fields to rely on:
  - `name`, `subject`, `sender`, `recipients`, `content`, `status`, `reference_doctype`, `reference_name`
  - `provider`, `provider_message_id`, `provider_thread_id`
- API payloads:
  - Agent router `email.draft`: `{ reference_doctype, reference_name, to, subject, html, cc?, bcc?, provider_thread_id? }`
  - Agent router `email.draft_with_provider`: `{ reference_doctype, reference_name, to, subject, html, provider?, provider_message_id?, provider_thread_id?, cc?, bcc? }`
  - Agent router `email.send`: `{ communication_name }`
  - `email.link_provider_ids`: `{ communication_name, provider?, provider_message_id?, provider_thread_id? }`

## Next Actions
1) EAIA service setup (local):
   - `pip install -e . && langgraph dev`
   - `python scripts/setup_gmail.py` (OAuth) and fill `eaia/main/config.yaml`
   - `python scripts/run_ingest.py --minutes-since 120 --rerun 1 --early 0`
2) EAIA → CRM wiring (use new one-call endpoint):
   - For each triaged thread, call `crm.api.agent.run` with `email.draft_with_provider`
3) Human review:
   - Review at `/human_inbox` (filter by `doctype`/`docname`/`only_drafts=1`), use Send action
4) Deliverability (backlog):
   - Add SPF/DKIM/DMARC; retest headers (SPF/DKIM/DMARC = PASS)
5) E2E tests:
   - Ingest → draft_with_provider → review → send → verify provider IDs present

## How to Use (Quick Reference)
- Create draft (EAIA one call):
  - `crm.api.agent.run` { command: `email.draft_with_provider`, params: {...} }
- Link IDs post-send:
  - `email.link_provider_ids` { communication_name, provider_message_id, provider_thread_id }
- Send from CRM:
  - `email.send` { communication_name }
- Review/Send UI:
  - `/human_inbox` or via `/crm` widget and Lead actions

## Ownership & Review Checklist
- CRM APIs: backend owner reviews payload validation, permissions, rate limits
- EAIA service: AI/ML owner reviews prompts, tools, auth, logs
- Security: verify secrets handling, scopes, and principle of least privilege
- Deliverability: ensure SPF/DKIM/DMARC for sending domain

## Rollout Plan
1) Enable in staging with a test Gmail
2) Run EAIA locally against staging CRM; validate IDs and timelines
3) Promote EAIA to LangGraph; configure cron
4) Enable notifications + Human Inbox for selected users
5) Production rollout with observability (Email Queue failures, API error logs)

